<!-- ╔══════════════════════════════════════════╗ -->
<!-- ║  WHY ELECTROLYTES MATTER                 ║ -->
<!-- ╚══════════════════════════════════════════╝ -->
<div class="ec-sci-block ec-sci-why">
  <div class="ec-container">

    <div class="ec-sci-block-header">
      <div class="ec-sci-label">Why electrolytes matter</div>
    </div>

    <div class="ec-sci-cards">

      <div class="ec-sci-card">
        <div class="ec-sci-card-num" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
        <h3 class="ec-sci-card-title">You lose all four in every workout</h3>
        <p class="ec-sci-card-body">Sweat contains sodium, potassium, calcium, and magnesium. As exercise intensity increases, your body's electrolyte reserves decline — raising the risk of cramps, fatigue, and impaired performance.</p>
        <div class="ec-sci-cite">HORIBA / Baker et al., 2014</div>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-sci-card">
        <div class="ec-sci-card-num" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
        <h3 class="ec-sci-card-title">A 2% drop changes everything</h3>
        <p class="ec-sci-card-body">Losing as little as 2% of body mass through dehydration produces a measurable decrease in endurance, strength, and cognitive ability — even before you feel thirsty.</p>
        <div class="ec-sci-cite">Nix Biosensors, citing peer-reviewed research</div>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-sci-card">
        <div class="ec-sci-card-num" aria-hidden="true">03</div>
        <h3 class="ec-sci-card-title">Plain water isn't enough</h3>
        <p class="ec-sci-card-body">Electrolytes help the body absorb water more effectively than plain water alone, and replace the essential minerals lost through sweat that water simply can't restore.</p>
        <div class="ec-sci-cite">Edith Cowan University / ScienceDaily, 2021</div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ╔══════════════════════════════════════════╗ -->
<!-- ║  THE FOUR MINERALS                       ║ -->
<!-- ╚══════════════════════════════════════════╝ -->
<div class="ec-sci-block ec-sci-minerals-block">
  <div class="ec-container">

    <div class="ec-sci-block-header">
      <div class="ec-sci-label">The four minerals in every piece</div>
    </div>

    <div class="ec-sci-minerals">

      <div class="ec-sci-mineral">
        <div class="ec-sci-tile">
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-num">19</div>
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-sym">K</div>
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-name">Potassium</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ec-sci-mineral-body">
          <h3 class="ec-sci-mineral-title">Potassium</h3>
          <p class="ec-sci-mineral-desc">During intense exercise, potassium shifts out of muscle cells into the bloodstream and is lost through sweat — slowing recovery and making it harder for muscles to rebuild and repair.</p>
          <div class="ec-sci-cite">Wellbeing Nutrition / sports science literature</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-sci-mineral">
        <div class="ec-sci-tile ec-sci-tile--2">
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-num">12</div>
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-sym">Mg</div>
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-name">Magnesium</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ec-sci-mineral-body">
          <h3 class="ec-sci-mineral-title">Magnesium</h3>
          <p class="ec-sci-mineral-desc">Research links optimal magnesium levels to grip strength, leg power, knee torque, and jumping performance. It activates the sodium-potassium pump that drives water and nutrients into your cells. Without enough of it, the other electrolytes can't fully do their job.</p>
          <div class="ec-sci-cite">NIH / PMC, 2017</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-sci-mineral">
        <div class="ec-sci-tile ec-sci-tile--3">
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-num">20</div>
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-sym">Ca</div>
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-name">Calcium</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ec-sci-mineral-body">
          <h3 class="ec-sci-mineral-title">Calcium</h3>
          <p class="ec-sci-mineral-desc">Calcium regulates muscle contraction at the cellular level. Alongside magnesium, it plays a foundational role in muscle mass and physical functioning — and both are associated with long-term performance outcomes.</p>
          <div class="ec-sci-cite">PMC / National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey, 2020</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-sci-mineral">
        <div class="ec-sci-tile ec-sci-tile--4">
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-num">11</div>
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-sym">Na</div>
          <div class="ec-sci-tile-name">Sodium</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ec-sci-mineral-body">
          <h3 class="ec-sci-mineral-title">Sodium <span class="ec-sci-mineral-subtitle">Pink Himalayan Salt</span></h3>
          <p class="ec-sci-mineral-desc">A trace amount of sodium — sourced from pink Himalayan salt — supports fluid retention and helps initiate muscle contractions. We keep it modest by design: enough to support the formula, not enough to make you bloated or reliant on a sodium hit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>

