    <div class="ec-sci-delivery">

      <div class="ec-sci-delivery-text">
        <h2 class="ec-sci-delivery-headline">Buccal absorption:<br>the science behind the chew</h2>
        <p class="ec-sci-delivery-body">When you swallow a drink or powder, it has to travel through your entire digestive system before reaching your bloodstream — a process that can take 30 minutes or more. ElectroChew works differently. Chewing activates the release of the electrolyte formula across the soft tissue inside your mouth, where absorption into the bloodstream can begin within 5–10 minutes — bypassing the GI tract entirely.</p>
        <p class="ec-sci-delivery-body">This is the same well-established delivery mechanism used in medical and pharmaceutical applications — from nicotine gum to nitroglycerin tablets — where speed of absorption matters. Published research in <em>Frontiers in Pharmacology</em> confirms that buccal and sublingual routes produce faster onset of action than orally ingested formulations, and that absorbed compounds enter systemic circulation directly, skipping first-pass liver metabolism.</p>
      </div>

